## 2. What was built (new files only, shared modules untouched)

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/ZenRayMotionDesign/zrmd/audio/stems/bass.py` | `tonal_note_fit`: sms.tonal_note plus per-note `releaseS` (T60), low-pass tilt `tiltDbOct` above `cornerHz`, `attackDb`, `sustainDb` (from 60 ms, 40 ms crossfade) and an optional per-note third-octave gain `bandDb` (21 centres 30 Hz to 3 kHz, clipped to 12 dB). Neutral values reproduce V_034 bit for bit. `chain` replays residual, per-bar equaliser, automation (adaptive or a frozen fader lane) and stereo exactly as `resynth.render`. Two fit models in the critic's frame domain: `BandModel` (power sum, no cross terms) and `ComplexModel` (complex critic frames per note, cross terms included, starts exactly at the critic's E). `fit_fader` / `fit_fader_c` refit the fader lane point by point. |
| `/Users/zenray/.claude/tmp/tmp-zenray-motion-design/ZenRayMotionDesign/Scripts/IterateBass.py` | `selftest`, `run` (steps `neutral`, `freeze`, `fit`, `fit:<keys>`, `fader`, `remeasure`, options `--resume`, `--revert`, `--model power|complex`), `mix`. Each step writes a new `stem-iter/bass/V_NNN`. |

Interface (HDA): `FIT` in `bass.py` (neutral values, grids, sustain start and ramp, band centres and grid, sweeps) and `CFG` in `IterateBass.py` (target, plateau, fader grid and sweeps, model). Every version's `params.json` holds the per-note fits (`notes`, keyed `role:index`), the fader lane `faderDb` (dB per 50 ms automation hop), and the stem `eq` and `residual` it was rendered with.

