## 6. What the measurements taught

1. The release, tilt and sustain fit alone gave only +0.19 (97.71 to 97.90) while the adaptive automation stayed on: it rides the RMS every 50 ms toward the lane and undoes level changes. Freezing the lane and fitting it against the critic error (the fader step) gave +0.69 at once.
2. The power-sum model overrates the fits (cross terms between repeated notes of one pitch, which this bass plays constantly); the complex-frame model is exact at its starting point and crossed 99 in one step.
3. Fitted shapes: median release 0.08 s (the voice macro was 0.25 s, confirming the M3 diagnosis of too long a release), median tilt 3 dB/oct above 1 kHz, median attack +1 dB, sustain median 0 dB with a range of -9 to +6 dB.
4. The 2 to 6 kHz overshoot (+1.9 dB, 4 percent of the error) does not come from the notes (the voice stops at 3 kHz); it comes from the residual bed and the per-bar equaliser. It is the next lever only if a stricter score is wanted.

